# Copy to apps/web/.op/refs.env (gitignored) or export OP_ENVIRONMENT_ID in your shell.
#
# Create Environments in *your* 1Password account (Developer → Environments).
# Suggested display names (not shared project vaults to request access to):
#
#   amigo (dev)  — your local `pnpm run dev` / Cursor Cloud Agents
#   amigo (prod) — your Cloudflare Workers Builds deploy (operators only)
#
# Populate required keys from apps/web/.dev.vars.example with your own Clerk
# credentials (APP_ENV, APP_ORIGIN, CLERK_*). Cloudflare IDs and VAPID are
# optional for local Vite. Deploy manifests are for operators only.
#
# Cursor Cloud Agents: do not copy apps/web/.op/refs.env or individual app secrets into
# Cursor. Set only AMIGO_OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN + AMIGO_OP_ENVIRONMENT_ID for *your*
# Environment — see README § Cursor Cloud Agents. Cursor secret names are global across
# repos, so they must stay amigo-prefixed. Local shells and Workers Builds keep OP_*.
#
# Use the Environment UUID from 1Password, not the display name.
OP_ENVIRONMENT_ID=
